\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF: No change in  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  policy  \b0\par\par\uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2006\par 02:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, details)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made no change in its policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and Tokyo will act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has not been changed at all," Masatsugu Asakawa, director of the MOF's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market division, told a seminar in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 He said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since March 2004 but would act "whenever we feel it necessary". "So please don't feel too relaxed," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Asakawa also said there was no reason for the yen to rise in tandem with the Chinese yuan.  \par \par \uc2 He reiterated the ministry's mantra that Japan has no intention of diverting its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves out of the U.S. dollar into other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Shifting out of the dollar would mean Tokyo would have to sell dollars for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that could lead to an "unforeseeable fluctuation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market", Asakawa said.  \par \par \uc2 "It would be completely inconsistent with our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  (policy)," Asakawa added.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not give a breakdown of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its foreign reserves, which were the world's largest at $851.666 billion at the end of January, but most of the reserves are believed to be in U.S. dollars.  \par \par \uc2 While Japan historically has tended to make money on its yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and later selling them at higher prices, Asakawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is not aimed at seeking profits and its sole purpose is to avoid fluctuation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 When Japan was trying prevent a soaring yen from derailing its nascent export-led recovery a few years ago, it bought a record 20 trillion yen worth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- predominantly dollars -- for yen in 2003 and a further 15 trillion yen worth in the first three months of 2004.  \par \par \uc2 But since then, it has refrained from making forays into the market, not least because the yen has been declining on its own accord, thanks to rock-bottom Japanese interest rates that contrast with rising U.S. rates.  \par \par \uc2 An absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  meant \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves would be little changed -- unlike China's, which have been rapidly expanding as Beijing fights persistent upward pressure on the yuan under its "managed float" regime.  \par \par \uc2 China's reserves rose to $818.9 billion at the end of 2005, up nearly $50 billion in the October-December quarter. At that pace, they would eclipse Japan's in the first half of this year.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-JAPAN-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|J|NAT|E|U|Z|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060223e22n0003n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
