\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Yen volatile but within fundamentals-Tanigaki  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Ritsuko Ando  \par \uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2006\par 00:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates market moves)  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jan 8 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Sunday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had been volatile of late although it still largely reflected fundamentals, suggesting the government was wary of the yen's rise but in no rush to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "I do not comment on specific levels, but I would say they are largely within fundamentals. But sometimes, with trade thin around the new year, there have been wild moves and such," he told Reuters after arriving in New York for a week-long visit to the United States.  \par \par \uc2 His comments helped accelerate a fall in the dollar to a three-month low of about 113.78 yen in early Asian trade on Monday. Around 0435 GMT, dollar/yen was quoted at around 113.90. Trade was thin with Japanese markets closed for a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell on Friday after the U.S. jobs report for December came in much weaker than expected, which bolstered expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve was close to ending its monetary tightening.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has been on a weaker trend in the past week after minutes from the Fed's last policy-setting meeting confirmed perceptions that an expected rate rise at the Jan. 31 policy meeting could well be the last for now.  \par \par \uc2 FUNDAMENTALS, VOLATILITY  \par \par \uc2 Although Japan's economy has recovered over the past year, the government is still worried that too strong a yen could hurt exporters' earnings and prolong deflation.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo spent a record 35 trillion yen in 2003 and the first three months of 2004 combined to stem the yen's rise. It has stayed out of the market since March 2004.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has two standard refrains -- that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should be in line with economic fundamentals and that movements should not be too volatile.  \par \par \uc2 Sean Callow, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac in Singapore, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared happy with a wide range in dollar/yen.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken a pretty clear step away from active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki is due to give a speech at the Japan Society on Monday before visiting Washington for meetings with U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow, Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan and other top officials.  \par \par \uc2 The meetings with leading U.S. figures may help raise his political profile ahead of this year's election for the head of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party, a job that also carries with it the prime ministership.  \par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi steps down in September. (Additional reporting by Dhara Ranasinghe)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-JAPAN-TANIGAKI (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|J|NAT|U|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060108e218000k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
