\par\par \b \uc2 IMF urges more China  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  moves as cenbankers meet  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anchalee Worrachate and Thomas Atkins  \par \uc2 816 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2006\par 22:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  BASEL, Switzerland, Jan 8 (Reuters) - China needs to take further steps to loosen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, the International Monetary Fund chief said on Sunday as top central bankers met on the outlook for emerging markets in 2006.  \par \par \uc2  Asian countries are worried that upward pressure on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  compared with China's will hurt otherwise strong growth prospects this year.  \par \par \uc2  China announced last week fresh steps towards allowing markets to set some rates for the yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its tightly managed floating rate system, adopted last July. But IMF Managing Director Rodrigo Rato said more needs to be done.  \par \par \uc2  "We see the importance of the Chinese government and the Chinese authorities to make more use of that flexibility and to make their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a clearer reflection of the market forces," he told Reuters at the Bank for International Settlements here.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Chinese yuan, will be on Monday's agenda for the global economy discussion among central bankers from top industrialised and emerging nations, who meet six times a year here at the BIS.  \par \par \uc2  Many Asian countries are enjoying strong growth. But they are worried that China's tightly managed yuan trading band, a weaker U.S. dollar and strong investor demand for Asian assets are putting too much upward pressure on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which could threaten their exports and hurt growth.  \par \par \uc2  South Korea vowed on Friday to clamp down and stabilise the market after its won \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit an 8-year high at 985.1 <KRW=> last week and has risen 3 percent this year. Bank of Korea Governor Park Seung would not comment at the BIS meetings.  \par \par \uc2  Taiwan and Singapore already have sold dollars to counter a month-long rally in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Vice Finance Minister Hiroshi Watanabe hinted at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by saying the yen's <JPY=> advance was "rough". The U.S. dollar has slid 1.5 percent against the yen this year alone.  \par \par \uc2  But Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said he did not view the movements in his \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as too rapid.  \par \par \uc2  "We are seeing ... perhaps some unwinding of carry trades ... but not too much volatility," Fukui said.  \par \par \uc2  In the carry trade, investors borrowed very cheaply in Japan, which pursues a zero interest-rate policy along with liquidity injections to combat stubborn deflation. Japan is expected to end its liquidity injections some time this year.  \par \par \uc2  STRONG OUTLOOK, DESPITE RISKS  \par \par \uc2  Overall, central bankers reviewing the health of emerging market economies in a Sunday session, concluded they are in good condition, said Argentina's governor Martin Redrado.   \par \par \uc2  "Macroeconomic conditions in emerging markets are very strong. Fiscal conditions are very strong. External positions are very strong. Most of the countries in the emerging world have a fiscal surplus and a current account surplus," he said.  \par \par \uc2  Latin America looks set for 4.3 percent average growth this year, and pending presidential elections should not upset government promises to follow sound economic policies, he said.  \par \par \uc2  In a separate meeting, commercial bankers explored potential threats to financial stability. Rijkman Groenink, CEO of Dutch bank ABN AMRO  called it an "important exchange" with central bankers on risk management and other regulatory issues.  \par \par \uc2  Though the outlook is benign, central bankers said a litany of risks remain that could upset the global economy-- another spurt in crude oil costs, a sharp change in asset prices and further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate rises.  \par \par \uc2  Speaking on Dutch television, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governing Council member Nout Wellink held out the prospect for another ECB rate hike given an improving euro-zone economy.  \par \par \uc2  "It is clear that with, let us say given inflation expectations, as the European economy strengthens, the chances for a further rate rise increase," said Wellink. The ECB meets next Thursday but is expected to stay on hold.  \par \par \uc2  Jaime Caruana, ECB governor from Spain, described the December 0.25 percentage point rate hike to 2.25 percent, its first in five years, as a "minor change" and said he needs more time to assess its effect on Spain's hot housing market.  \par \par \uc2  Another factor Wellink added to the list of global dangers is the rapidly escalating U.S. trade and budget deficits.  \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. deficit on its balance of payments is heading towards 7 percent ... We looked back 200 years and this is unprecedented. We are worried about it and talking about it in international forums such as the G10," he said.  \par \par \uc2  The United States must suck in $3 billion a day to finance its current account deficit, and investor reluctance to invest in U.S. assets could lead to a disruptive dollar correction.  (Additional reporting by Wendell Broere in Amsterdam and Stella Dawson in Basel)    \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-CENTRALBANKERS|LANGEN|ABN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|ABX|BNX|FUN|Z|J|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060108e218000he\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
