\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won ends lower, tracking weaker yen  \b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2005\par 02:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Dec 19 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> edged lower in domestic trade on Monday, closing at a session low, hit by heavy equity sales by foreign investors and as the yen dipped following verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister.  \par \par \uc2 Data showing a narrower-than-expected U.S. current account deficit in the third quarter also spurred dollar short-covering in afternoon trade, as investors bet the worst of last week's dollar sell-off was over.  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=KFTC> settled at 1,017.7 per dollar, down 0.15 percent from Friday's local close of 1,016.2. It opened at 1,016.0 and hit a session high of 1,013.4.  \par \par \uc2 "The key test will occur at 1,018 won, a five-day moving average. Given the current mood, 1,020 won could be tested once or twice," said a dealer at a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said the Tokyo government was carefully monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, a move seen aimed at curbing a firmer yen.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar suffered its worst weekly loss to the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six years last week, falling more than 4 percent as traders reversed big bets against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers saw some short-term upside potential for the dollar, which hit a seven-week low of around 115 per yen <JPY=> earlier in the day.  \par \par \uc2 But potential dollar sales by South Korean exporters, who missed out on selling the U.S. unit at 1,030 earlier this month, might hamper the dollar's upward trend in the longer term, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar shed 1.7 percent versus the won last week.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors sold a net 273 billion won worth of local equities on the main exchange. The benchmark stock index <.KS11> finished 1.39 percent higher.  \par \par \uc2 The won found some early support on expectations of demand for the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Japan's NTT DoCoMo agreed last week to buy a stake in local mobile operator KTF Co. Ltd. .  \par \par \uc2 The two firms agreed on Thursday DoCoMo would buy the shares for 565 billion won.  \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=>, which the won usually follows closely, was quoted at 116.51/53 per dollar versus 116.01/04 late on Friday in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by $1.77 billion during the first half of December as a weaker dollar boosted the value of assets held in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. [ID:nSEO341073]  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                      0647 GMT       0041 GMT    prev close\par  Won <KRW=KFTC>          1,017.7        1,013.9       1,016.2\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>    8.7378/25      8.7622/62     8.7692/47\par  NDF 1-mth won       1,016.9/7.9    1,013.3/4.3   1,015.5/6.5\par  NDF 3-mth won       1,016.1/7.1    1,012.6/3.6   1,014.8/5.8\par  KOSPI <.KS11>          1,339.40       1,330.31      1,321.04\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051222e1cj000a7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
