\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX- \highlight22\uc2 Japan forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 630 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 November 2005\par 09:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 16 (Reuters) - Since its move to a floating exchange rate system in February 1973, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market periodically to smooth out rapid changes in the value of the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, since a 15-month spree of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that ended in mid-March 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Now, with the yen mired at a 27-month low against the dollar, some analysts are considering the possibility \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the opposite direction to support the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Below is an explanation of how \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a timeline of some of its biggest forays into the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market over the last decade.  \par \par \uc2 HOW \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) is authorised to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its behalf.  \par \par \uc2 - Funds needed for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  come from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Special Account (FEFSA).  \par \par \uc2 - In the case of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in which a foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is bought and yen sold, the MOF raises yen funds to be sold by issuing financing bills (FBs).  \par \par \uc2 - In the case of yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the BOJ sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the FEFSA. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had foreign reserves of $841.792 billion as of the end of October, the largest in the world. The bulk of these holdings is believed to be in dollars.  \par \par \uc2 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is usually conducted in the Tokyo market, but if it is seen necessary to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in U.S. or European trading hours the BOJ will either do so itself or MOF will ask foreign monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its behalf.  \par \par \uc2 RECENT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 - Japanese authorities have not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since March 16, 2004, when they bought dollars after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had fallen nearly two yen on the day to around 108.60 yen  \par \par \uc2 - Japan sold around 25 trillion yen ($210.2 billion) in the 15 months to March 2004, aiming to stop any sharp rise in the yen from derailing a fragile export-led economic recovery and helping to battle deflation.  \par \par \uc2 - The MOF last conducted dollar-selling/yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 17, 1998, when it bought 231.2 billion yen as the dollar traded just above 144 yen.  \par \par \uc2 - At that time Japan had just suffered a severe recession and was grappling with a banking crisis. As a vote of confidence, the U.S. also sold dollars for yen that day.  \par \par \uc2 - The MOF also sold dollars for yen on April 9-10, 1998, when it bought 2.8 trillion yen as the dollar was trading at around 131.50-133.50 yen.  \par \par \uc2 - The MOF bought 1.06 trillion yen on Dec. 17-19, 1997, helping push the dollar from around 131.50 yen to as low as just under 126 yen.  \par \par \uc2 - It also bought around 700 billion yen in a sustained bout of dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April-August 1992, helping prod the yen from around 135 to the dollar to near 125.  \par \par \uc2 - While the bulk of MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been via the dollar, as recently as May 2003 it sold yen for euros. Japan also bought Indonesian rupiah in late 1997 at the height of the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis.  \par \par \uc2 TOP FIVE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  VOLUMES  \par \par \uc2 Following is a list of the top five days for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume since 1991, based on MOF figures:  \par \par \uc2 1. April 10, 1998: 2.6201 trln yen  \par \par \uc2 (dollar selling, yen buying)  \par \par \uc2 2. Jan. 9, 2004: 1.6664 trln yen  \par \par \uc2 (dollar buying, yen selling)  \par \par \uc2 3. June 14, 1999: 1.4059 trln yen  \par \par \uc2 (dollar buying, yen selling)  \par \par \uc2 4. April 3, 2000: 1.3854 trln yen  \par \par \uc2 (dollar buying, yen selling)  \par \par \uc2 5. Sept. 21, 2001: 1.2874 trln yen  \par \par \uc2 (dollar buying, yen selling) ($1=118.94 Yen)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051116e1bg000py\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
