\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Holds Largest  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Reserves For 71st Month In August  \b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2005\par 04:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan remained holder of the world's largest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for the 71st straight month in August, according to data from the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves totaled $837.11 billion in August, the IMF said. Mainland China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves came in second at $714.58 billion in July, the IMF said. July is the earliest month IMF data are available for China.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data from the IMF differ from those issued by Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to differences in the methods used to calculate the value of gold.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves have shown only minor changes in line with asset price and exchange rate fluctuations since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped its campaign of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March last year.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Stanley White, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; stanley.white@dowjones.com \par    -Edited by Shawn Schroter \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-11-05 0341GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051108e1b80004m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
