\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Japan Oct Foreign Reserves Down $1.77B On Month  \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2005\par 02:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Updates to add more details.) \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves fell $1.77 billion on month in October to $841.79 billion as the value of the country's U.S. bond holdings and euro-denominated assets fell, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The decrease in reserves, which include convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights, follows a $4.2 billion fall in September and an $8.39 billion rise in August.  \par \par \uc2 Gains in the yield on long-term foreign bonds decreased the value of Japan's government bond holdings in October and contributed to the fall in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, a MOF official told reporters at a briefing.  \par \par \uc2 Bond yields move inversely to prices, so a rise in the yield means a fall in the price, and therefore a fall in the value of such bond holdings.  \par \par \uc2 The bulk of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are believed to be held in the form of U.S. Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of October, 10-year Treasurys yielded 4.555%, up from 4.328% at the end of September, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro's decline versus the dollar also reduced the value of euro-denominated assets in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was quoted at $1.1992 in New York at the end of October, down from $1.2026 at the end of the previous month, according to data from the MOF.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have shown only minor changes in line with asset price and exchange rate fluctuations since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped its campaign of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March last year.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF also confirmed Tuesday that it spent no money on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the July-September period.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Stanley White, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; stanley.white@dowjones.com \par    -Edited by Hugh Lawson \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 08-11-05 0132GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051108e1b80002a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
