\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan foreign reserves $841.792 bln at end-Oct  \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2005\par 00:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds MOF comment)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 8 (Reuters) - Japan's official reserves, the world's largest, edged down to $841.792 billion at the end of October from $843.563 billion a month earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign reserves have fallen slightly since rising to a record high of $847.766 billion in August.  \par \par \uc2 Still, the October figure is the seventh-highest on record.  \par \par \uc2 "The largest factor behind the fall in reserves was a sharp rise in U.S. yields, which boosted book losses on a mark-to-market basis," a senior MOF official said.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on benchmark 10-year notes <US10YT=RR>, which rise when prices fall, climbed 26 basis points in October to 4.56 percent at the end of October. The yield was at 4.61 percent in early Asia on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 A fall in the euro also decreased the dollar-value of euro-denominated reserves, the official said. The euro was fetching $1.1782 <EUR=> in early Tokyo trade.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves had ballooned after yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a record 20 trillion yen ($169.9 billion) in 2003 and a further 15 trillion yen in the first three months of 2004.  \par \par \uc2 However, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since then.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the largest foreign reserves in the world, although China is quickly closing the gap. China \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market under its new managed float system that has kept its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading near 8.09 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 China's foreign reserves rose to $769 billion by the end of September from $711 billion at the end of June. ($1=117.71 Yen) [20051107 235213 GMT]  \par \par \uc2 [20051108 004732 GMT]   \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-JAPAN-RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|J|ABN|M|D|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD|ECONOMY-JAPAN-RESERVES (UPDATE 1) =2|LANGEN|J|ABN|M|D|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD|chained  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051107e1b7002bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
