\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  not mulling yen-buying  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -govt  \b0\par\par\uc2 187 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2005\par 10:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not considering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as the yen fell to its lowest levels against the dollar in two years on Tuesday, the top government spokesman said.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think it is being considered," Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiroyuki Hosoda told reporters when asked whether the government had any plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market amid a weaker yen and high oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 Japan imports almost all of its oil, and a weaker yen raises the cost.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was last trading at around 115.56 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Tokyo has refrained from entering the market since March 2004, when it sold yen for dollar to stem a rising yen.  \par \par \uc2 The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in 1998, when the yen fell to around 146 yen to the dollar.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is run by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  merely acting as its agent in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-JAPAN-HOSODA|LANGEN|J|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051018e1ai000je\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
