\par\par \b \uc2 Ex-Japan MOF Mizoguchi:G7 Approach To  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Well Balanced  \b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 September 2005\par 18:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--A former top Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Sunday the Group of Seven monetary officials took a balanced approach to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates by welcoming China's reforms but expressing expectations for further developments.  \par \par \uc2 "The G7's approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was reasonable, and was well-balanced," said Zembei Mizoguchi, who was vice finance minister for international affairs until last year, and is now president of the Japan Center for International Finance.  \par \par \uc2 "It continues to touch on the need for exchange rates to reflect fundamentals and how disorderly movements are undesirable, but it also takes into account China's recent efforts to increase flexibility," Mizoguchi told Dow Jones Newswires on the sidelines of a conference sponsored by the Institute for International Finance in Washington.  \par \par \uc2 At the same time, the statement also properly underscores the international community's desire to see more flexibility in China's yuan exchange rate, he said.  \par \par \uc2 The statement, while welcoming Beijing's efforts so far on the yuan, also says that the G7 members "expect the development of this more market-oriented system to improve the functioning and stability of the global economy and the international monetary system."  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi noted, however, that Beijing would likely take a gradual approach to reform - as indicated by comments from Chinese officials this weekend - considering domestic problems that must be resolved.  \par \par \uc2 In July, China ended its practice of pegging its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the U.S. dollar and instead began targeting a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Then Friday, China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took a further step toward flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, widening the daily band in which the yuan can trade against the Japanese yen, Hong Kong dollar and euro to 3% above and below the previous day's closing level, up from 1.5%.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi said that the latest moves were only technical, and were unlikely to largely affect \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading.  \par \par \uc2 On Saturday, Mizoguchi's successor, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Hiroshi Watanabe, told reporters he was unhappy over China's latest move and feels it should be corrected over the long term.  \par \par \uc2 "It's unreasonable that there is now a 10-fold difference between the yuan's trading band against the dollar and the band against non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially given the fact the non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  aren't minor," Watanabe said. "The bands should be the same" for all \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Watanabe's comments likely reflect Japan's concerns that if the dollar is controlled in a tight band against the yuan while the yen is allowed to move more, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may come under stronger upward pressure in the event of a yuan fall.  \par \par \uc2 That may also prompt speculators to drive the yen higher against the dollar, regardless of Japanese and U.S. economic fundamentals. Japan has long maintained exchange rates should reflect economic fundamentals, and has in the past \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when it felt markets were behaving in an unruly way.  \par \par \uc2 Mizoguchi, who was in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign of January 2003-March 2004 aimed at fighting undue yen strength, said, however, that as the trading volumes of the dollar, the euro and the yen are much greater than that of the yuan, the dollar/yuan rate won't have much effect on the dollar/yen rate.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 202-216-9720; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-25-05 1216ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020050925e19p00034\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
