\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:Japan August Foreign Reserves Rise To Record High  \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2005\par 02:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose $8.39 billion in August to $847.77 billion, marking a new record high, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which include convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights, follows a $4.16 billion fall in July and a $1.07 billion rise in June. Current reserves exceeded the previous high of $844.54 billion marked in December of last year.  \par \par \uc2 Falling U.S. Treasury yields increased the value of Japan's government bond holdings, leading to the rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, a MOF official told reporters at a briefing. The bulk of Japan's foreign reserves are thought to be held in Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of August, the 10-year Treasury yield was 4.035%, down from 4.280% at the end of July, according to the official.  \par \par \uc2 The euro's rise against the dollar also increased the value of Japan's euro-denominated assets, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was quoted at $1.2346 at the end of August, up from $1.2122 at the end of July, according to MOF data.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have shown only minor changes corresponding to asset price and exchange rate fluctuations since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in March of last year.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained the holder of the world's largest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for the 69th straight month in June, which is the latest month for which data are available from the IMF.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves in the month totaled $834.0 billion, according to the IMF. China ranked second with $696.0 billion in reserves in May, the latest month for which it has released data. Taiwan's reserves were third at $253.6 billion in June.  \par \par \uc2 Data from the IMF differ slightly from those issued by the MOF due to differences in methods used to calculate the value of gold.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Jay Alabaster [ 07-09-05 0059GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050907e19700013\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
