\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan external reserves swell to record in August  \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2005\par 01:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 7 (Reuters) - Japan's official reserves grew to a record high at the end of August due to a rise in the prices of its U.S. Treasury holdings as well as a strengthening euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign reserves amounted to $847.766 billion, up from $839.378 billion a month earlier and surpassing the previous record of $844.543 billion in December 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has the largest foreign reserves in the world, although China is quickly closing the gap. China \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market under its new managed float system that has kept its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading around 8.09 to the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 China's foreign reserves rose to $711 billion by end-June from $609.90 billion at the end of 2004. Japan's have changed much less since over the same period.  \par \par \uc2 The fluctuations in Japan's reserves have been determined by swings in the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar and by interest income on foreign asset holdings.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves ballooned after yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a record 20 trillion yen ($182.5 billion) in 2003 and a further 15 trillion yen in the first three months of 2004. However, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since then. ($1=109.60 Yen) [20050906 235203 GMT]  \par \par \uc2 [20050907 003817 GMT]  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-JAPAN-RESERVES (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|J|ABN|M|D|NAT|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP|PTD|ECONOMY-JAPAN-RESERVES (UPDATE 1) =2|LANGEN|Table|J|ABN|M|D|NAT|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP|PTD|chained  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050907e19600011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
