\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  says didn't  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market in Aug  \b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2005\par 11:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during the month from July 28 to Aug. 29, marking the 17th straight month it has stayed out of the market.  \par \par \uc2 Japan sold a massive 35 trillion yen ($314 billion) in the 15 months to March 2004, fearing excessive yen strength could hurt exporters' profits and derail the fragile economy.  \par \par \uc2 But since then the economy has gradually recovered and expectations are high that stronger growth will help Japan pull out of its seven-year bout of deflation later this year or in early 2006.  \par \par \uc2 The yen has also weakened this year, falling 8 percent against the dollar since the start of the year as it backed away from a five-year high near 101.65 yen <JPY=> hit in January. The yen was trading around 111.50 to the dollar on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials have gone silent since the yen has weakened, after warning earlier in the year they were keeping an eye on the market, though they again said they were watching the market after China revalued the yuan on July 21.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts think the yen's fall this year means Tokyo authorities are unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near future.  \par \par \uc2 At the start of the new fiscal year in April, many large Japanese exporters said they were targeting a dollar/yen rate of about 105 yen and have been able to lock in even better levels for repatriating overseas profits.  \par \par \uc2 In the latest quarterly "tankan" survey of corporate sentiment by the Bank of Japan, firms said they expected the yen to trade closer to 104 per dollar during the April-September first half of the fiscal year.  \par \par \uc2 By some measures, the yen is very supportive of exports at current levels. A Bank of Japan index for the yen's performance against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of major trading partners hit a seven-year low in the first part of August.  \par \par \uc2 ($1=111.33 Yen)  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|U|M|D|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050831e18v000vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
