\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Confirms It Didn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  In August  \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2005\par 12:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities didn't take any action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for most of August, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday, marking the 17th straight month of inaction.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry said it didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from July 28 to Aug. 29, as market participants had expected.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell against the yen during the period, briefly dropping to a seven-week low of Y109.05 on Aug. 16. It later recouped some of the losses to move above Y110 for most of the rest of August, though that was still well below the month's high of Y112.67 marked Aug. 1.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since March 2004, when it ended a 15-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in which it had sold Y35 trillion, mostly for dollars, in a bid to keep a rise in the yen from snuffing out an economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data covered trades that are settled in August. Trades in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are settled after two business days.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson [ 31-08-05 1001GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokum