\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Japan July Foreign Reserves Fall As Yields Rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2005\par 03:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell $3.88 billion in July from June to $839.66 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday, as rising yields depressed the value of Japan's government bond holdings.  \par \par \uc2 The fall in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which include convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights, follows a $1.07 billion rise in June and a $1.13 billion decline in May.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent no money on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the April-June period, data from the MOF also showed.  \par \par \uc2 Since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in March last year, its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have shown only minor changes due to asset price and exchange rate fluctuations.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell in July for the first time in two months, because rising yields decreased the value of Japan's government bond holdings, a MOF official told reporters at a briefing. The bulk of Japan's foreign reserves are thought to be held in Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of July, 10-year Treasurys yielded 4.280%, up from 3.917% at the end of June, according to the official.  \par \par \uc2 The euro's recent rise against the dollar did increase the dollar-value of Japan's euro-denominated assets. However, this increase was not large enough to push Japan's overall reserves higher, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was quoted at $1.2122 at the end of July, up from $1.2107 at the end of June, according to MOF data.  \par \par \uc2 Japan remained the holder of the world's largest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for the 68th straight month in May, which is the latest month data are available from the IMF.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves in the month totaled $833.50 billion, according to the IMF. China ranked second with $675.90 billion in reserves in April. Taiwan's reserves were third at $253.90 billion in May.  \par \par \uc2 Data from the IMF differ slightly from those issued by the MOF due to differences in methods used to calculate the value of gold.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Stanley White, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; stanley.white@dowjones.com \par    -Edited by Shawn Schroter \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 05-08-05 0115GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050805e1850000y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
