\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Confirms It Didn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  In July  \b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 2005\par 12:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities didn't take any action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for most of July, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday, marking the 16th straight month of inaction.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry said it didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market between June 29 and July 27, as market participants had expected.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar strengthened against the yen during the period, gaining nearly four yen to touch a 14-month high of Y113.73 on July 20.  \par \par \uc2 There was talk in the market that the MOF may have stepped in to stem yen rises against the dollar when China announced suddenly on July 21 that it will no longer peg the yuan to the U.S. dollar but instead let it float in a tight band against a basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit briefly tumbled about two yen on the news to a low of Y109.87 but soon recovered and bounced back to near Y113 in a week.  \par \par \uc2 The data show the ministry didn't play a part in the dollar's rally, staying clear since mid-March last year, when it ended a 15-month yen-selling campaign in which it spent a thumping Y35 trillion to keep a rapid yen rise from hurting the economy.  \par \par \uc2 The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data covered trades that are settled in July. Trades in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are settled after two business days.  \par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com- tagline  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson [ 29-07-05 1002GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050729e17t000jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
