\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Japan Jun  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves Rise As Tsy Yields Fall  \b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2005\par 05:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose for the first time in two months in June, the government said Thursday, as a decline in yields on 10-year Treasurys inflated the value of the country's U.S. government bond holdings.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  also confirmed that it hasn't spent any money on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since it halted a record Y35 trillion campaign to weaken the yen in March last year.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in June rose $1.07 billion from the previous month to $843.54 billion, according to the MOF.  \par \par \uc2 The rise in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which includes convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights, follows a $1.13 billion decline in May and a $5.88 billion gain in April.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's foreign reserves in June were the third highest on record, following $843.60 billion in April and $844.54 billion in December, a MOF official told reporters at a briefing.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of June, the 10-year Treasury yield was 3.917%, down from 3.985% at the end of May, according to the official.  \par \par \uc2 Since bond prices move in the opposite direction of their yields, the value of Japan's U.S. government bond holdings rose, the official said. The bulk of Japan's foreign reserves are in Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 Increased earnings from other fixed income holdings also caused reserves to rise, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro's recent decline against the dollar decreased the dollar value of Japan's euro-denominated assets. However, this decline was not large enough to pull Japan's overall reserves lower, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was quoted at $1.2107 at the end of June, down from $1.2303 at the end of May, according to MOF data.  \par \par \uc2 Japan remained the world's largest holder of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for the 67th straight month in April, which is the latest month data are available from the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves in the month totaled $834.20 billion, according to the IMF. China ranked second with $664.20 billion in reserves in March. Taiwan's reserves were third at $253.90 billion in April.  \par \par \uc2 Data from the IMF differ slightly from those issued by the MOF due to differences in methods used to calculate the value of gold.  \par \par \uc2 Since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have shown only minor changes due to asset price and exchange rate fluctuations.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Stanley White, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; stanley.white@dowjones.com \par    -Edited by Shawn Schroter \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 07-07-05 0312GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050707e1770002x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
