\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Jun Foreign Reserves $843.54B; Up $1.07B On Month  \b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2005\par 01:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in June rose $1.07 billion from the previous month to $843.54 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The data underscore that the government has stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since it halted a massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign in March last year.  \par \par \uc2 The rise in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which includes convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights, follows a $1.13 billion decline in May and a $5.88 billion gain in April. [ 06-07-05 2353GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Japan's foreign reserves in June were the third highest on record, following $843.60 billion in April and $844.54 billion in December, a MOF official told reporters at a briefing.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose in June for the first time in two months, because falling yields on 10-year Treasurys inflated the value of Japan's U.S. government bond holdings, the official said. The bulk of Japan's foreign reserves are in Treasurys.  \par \par \uc2 At the end of June, the 10-year Treasury yield was 3.917%, down from 3.985% at the end of May, according to the official.  \par \par \uc2 Increased earnings from other fixed income holdings also caused reserves to rise, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro's recent decline against the dollar decreased the dollar-value of Japan's euro-denominated assets. However, this decline was not large enough to pull Japan's overall reserves lower, the official said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was quoted at $1.2107 at the end of June, down from $1.2303 at the end of May, according to MOF data.  \par \par \uc2 Since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign last March, its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have shown only minor changes due to asset price and exchange rate fluctuations.  \par \par \uc2 Japan remained the world's largest holder of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for the 67th straight month in April, which is the latest month data are available from the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves in the month totaled $834.20 billion, according to the IMF. China ranked second with $664.20 billion in reserves in March. Taiwan's reserves were third at $253.90 billion in April.  \par \par \uc2 Data from the IMF differ slightly from those issued by the MOF due to differences in methods used to calculate the value of gold.  \par \par \uc2 -By Stanley White, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; stanley.white@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Chris Gallagher [ 07-07-05 0039GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050706e176000yz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
