\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Oil big risk for Japan, global economy-BOJ  \b0\par\par\uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2005\par 18:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BASEL, Switzerland, June 26 (Reuters) - Japan's oil-reliant economy has weathered the impact from high energy prices so far but they pose a substantial risk for the domestic and global economy, Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said on Sunday.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters on the sidelines of the annual meeting of the Bank for International Settlements, Fukui reiterated the BOJ is committed to keep its four-year-old ultra easy policy until consumer prices rose.  \par \par \uc2 Surging oil prices, which have gained 60 percent over the past year to hit a record $60 a barrel for U.S. crude last week, have threatened to derail oil-dependent major and emerging economies.  \par \par \uc2 "We have come so far without big problems but if you ask me whether it is the source of a big problem I say it is relatively a big problem," Fukui said.  \par \par \uc2 Japan considers itself one of the most energy-efficient economies among industrialised nations. Nevertheless, it has been concerned about high oil prices indirectly hitting its export-driven economy if there is an oil-induced slowdown in the United States or China.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui said the outlook for China's red-hot economy also posed a risk for the world's second largest economy.  \par \par \uc2 "The Chinese economy is also a risk," he said.  \par \par \uc2 ULTRA EASY POLICY TO STAY  \par \par \uc2 Fukui painted an optimistic picture of Japan's economy, saying the economy on a path of a sustainable recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "The Japanese economy... is on track for a sustainable recovery," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "We are going to keep the easy monetary policy until the CPI comes up."  \par \par \uc2 Under its ultra-easy monetary policy, introduced in March 2001, the BOJ floods the money market to keep interest rates near zero.  \par \par \uc2 It has promised to keep the framework, introduced in March 2001, until year-on-year changes in consumer prices stabilise above zero.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ allowed funds in the banking system to stay below its 30-35 trillion yen target this month, seen as a symbolic first step towards an eventual end to its four-year ultra easy monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 But it has stressed such target breaches did not mean a monetary tightening because its fund-supplying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been under-subscribed for months as demand from healthier banks waned.  \par \par \uc2 Japan is suffering from seven-year-old deflation but the BOJ expects a 0.3 percent rise in the core consumer price index in fiscal 2006/2007 starting next April, which would be the first increase in nine years.  \par \par \uc2 YEN FLUCTUATIONS  \par \par \uc2 When asked about the yen, Fukui said: "(There were) not so great fluctuations these days, so (we are) not satisfied but we are watching future movements.  \par \par \uc2 In Japan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy is set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on behalf of the government.  \par \par \uc2 The yen hit a one-year high beyond 131 per euro <EURJPY=>, driven by general euro weakness.  \par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, it has fallen around 6 percent this year to trade around 109 yen <JPY=>, having hit a five-year high of 101.65 yen in January.  \par \par \uc2 With signs of a recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came to a halt in March 2004, after selling 35 trillion yen in the five quarters through the end of March 2004.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-BIS-JAPAN (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|J|ABX|BNX|FUN|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050626e16q0009p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
