\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  says did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market in May  \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2005\par 12:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Tuesday it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in May, marking the 14th straight month the MOF has stayed away since its aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign ended in March 2004.  \par \par \uc2 MOF data showed it refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from April 27 to May 27.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the MOF seems less worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels and that sudden, very sharp moves would be necessary for it to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki warned earlier this month that Japan would act against big yen moves stemming from speculative bets on a Chinese revaluation of the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 Such yuan speculation has died down in the past few weeks but helped spark a yen rally against the dollar from 108.90 yen in early April to as low as 104.15 yen in early May.  \par \par \uc2 The MOF last stepped into the market on March 16 last year when the dollar fell close to two yen on the day to around 108.60 yen <JPY=>.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities sold a record 20 trillion yen ($185 billion) in 2003 and another 15 trillion yen ($139 billion) in the first three months of 2004, fearing the yen's strength would hurt the economy.  \par \par \uc2 The yen fell to a six-week low against the dollar on Tuesday around 108.40 yen <JPY=> and remains weak against most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A Bank of Japan index of the yen's performance against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of major trading partners hit an eight-year low in April.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials also shied away from the market even as the yen hit a five-year high against the dollar around 101.65 yen earlier in the year. ($1=107.94 Yen)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-\b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|NAT|J|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050531e15v000uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
