\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Asia: Greenspan Yuan Comment To Keep Yen High Vs Dlr  \b0\par\par\uc2 944 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2005\par 09:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takeshi Takeuchi \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's public prompting of China to abandon its pegged \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  system continues to haunt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  players, who are reluctant to sell yen for dollars.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 While attention Monday was centered on conflicting signals over the weekend from Chinese monetary officials on when China might revalue the yuan, traders say it is Greenspan's remarks last week that are sustaining speculation that China will move soon.  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan said last Thursday in a Congressional testimony that Beijing should promptly "move off" the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, which virtually fixes the yuan at CNY8.28 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Any move by China to let the yuan rise is expected to put similar upward pressure on all Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "We cannot take lightly the fact that Greenspan, too (along with other U.S. leaders, including President George W. Bush), made such a direct comment," said Masaki Fukui, senior vice president of Mizuho Corporate Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division. "The market will remain wary about the possibility of yuan revaluation for the time being."  \par \par \uc2 That means \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players will be less responsive to dollar-bullish news when trading dollar/yen, keeping the exchange rate in a new lower range between Y104 and Y107 in coming days.  \par \par \uc2 At 0720 GMT, the greenback was quoted at Y105.82, down from Friday's close of Y106.50 in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    History Suggests Greenspan's Remarks Powerful \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some say that history shows Greenspan's public statements can eventually prove correct.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In March last year, for example, Greenspan criticized \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's aggressive dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that had totaled Y35 trillion in the previous 15 months.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the time, high-ranking Japanese government officials, such as then Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda, played down Greenspan's remark, saying it wasn't a "criticism" of Japan's policy.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But 10 days later, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stopped buying dollars and hasn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market since.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Japanese economic diplomat told Dow Jones Newswires at the time that "often in the past, (Greenspan's) seemingly casual remarks have later turned out to be something that set or changed the basic tenet of policies in the ensuing periods."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, it is unclear whether such "Greenspan magic" will work with China, a country that has different ways of dealing with the U.S. compared with Japan and has far less routine contact with Washington finance officials than the close U.S. ally.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some traders say what amounts to arm twisting by the U.S. will only harden China's opposition to a move, citing Chinese monetary officials' remarks over the weekend.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Zhou Xiaochuan Saturday acknowledged that the country is "making some preparations" for reform of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  system but said the process is "gradual" and that implementation is sequenced "according to the Chinese situation."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wei Benhua, vice director of China's State Administration of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , made clear China's displeasure with the recent U.S. demands.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This we cannot accept. I say this in a very blunt manner," Wei said at the same conference in Boao, China, where Zhou spoke.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Focus On U.S. Treasury Report \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But speculation of early action by China remains strong, despite the comments from Chinese officials.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The lineup of U.S. leaders that participated in the latest round of calls for China to act quickly gives Greenspan's remark special weight, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ahead of Greenspan, President Bush, Treasury Secretary John Snow and Undersecretary of Treasury for International Affairs John Taylor made similar demands.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The quartet is the highest of highest U.S. officials conceivable for this matter and none other than Greenspan made a grand finale" in calling on China to act, said Minoru Shioiri, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manager at Mitsubishi Securities.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The speculation (of early revaluation) won't fade easily, neither will the resulting market bullish sentiment for the yen against the dollar," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reflecting such market sentiment, one-year U.S. dollar/Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forward instrument that gauges market expectations of future moves in the yuan, on Monday dropped to the lowest level in over a year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The USD/CNY 1-year NDF was last bid at 4775 below spot after widening to as much as 5000 points earlier Monday, which was its lowest level since January 2004.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market participants are now focused on a U.S. Treasury Department semiannual report on trade and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is due as early as the end of this week, for a further possible prod by the U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Under the 1988 Trade Act, Treasury can formally identify in the report countries that manipulate their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for trade advantage. China was last named in 1994.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If Treasury again adds China to its list of manipulators, it would further fuel revaluation speculation and encourage a bullish outlook for the yen.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's hard to guess whether the Treasury would dare to name China," said Masamichi Koike, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot trading at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp. "But a (China) nomination would certainly be a factor that could send the yen higher against the dollar."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takeshi Takeuchi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; Takeshi.Takeuchi@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Takeshi Takeuchi has been Dow Jones Newswires' Tokyo bureau deputy chief in charge of macroeconomic policy and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . He has covered Japan's macroeconomic and trade policy, as well as politics, since the early 1980s, including a 2001-2004 stint in Washington covering Asian news from the IMF.)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Iain McDonald [ 25-04-05 0755GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 4258 5095  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050425e14p000bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picsca