\par\par \b \uc2 Japan March Foreign Reserves $837.72B; Down $2.85B On Mo  \b0\par\par\uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2005\par 01:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell $2.85 billion on month in March to $837.72 billion, marking the third straight month of decline, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The decrease in Japan's reserves of convertible foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gold and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights followed a contraction of $402 million in February and a decline of $3.58 billion in January.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's reserves, which ballooned during the MOF's aggressive yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign of January 2003-March 2004, have since posted only minor fluctuations on the back of interest income, asset price fluctuations and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate valuation losses or gains.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the MOF made public its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves policies for the first time, saying that it aims to ensure asset liquidity and prevent disruptions to financial markets.  \par \par \uc2 The ministry said the government's main objective in managing reserves is to make sure they include ample liquidity so they can be easily used for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the official said. While the MOF can finance yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by issuing short-term financing bills, if it wants to conduct dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it must use its reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Thursday's data also showed Japan's reserves remain the largest in the world.  \par \par \uc2 Japan's foreign reserves were the highest in the world for the 64th straight month in January, which is the latest month for which comparable data is available, the MOF said.  \par \par \uc2 According to data compiled by the International Monetary Fund, Japan had $831.9 billion in reserves in January, with China ranking second with $615.5 billion in December.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Kirsty Mackenzie  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corrected April 6, 2005 20:21 ET (00:21 GMT) [ 06-04-05 2359GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  must use its foreign reserves to conduct dollar-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ("\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  March Foreign Reserves $837.72B; Down $2.85B On Mo," published at 2359 GMT, incorrectly said the MOF must use foreign reserves if it wants to conduct dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .) [ 07-04-05 0019GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050406e1460011e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
